  "id": "innervation-ratio",
  "term": "innervation ratio",
  "definition": "Innervation ratio is a measure of the relative contribution of different nerves or regenerating axons to a muscle’s nerve supply. In this context, it is used to assess how much muscle reinnervation comes from the original nerve versus a donor nerve after nerve transfer or repair.",
