      "reasons": [
        "The packet never defines what “innervation ratio” numerically represents (e.g., as a relative contribution of different nerves or regenerating axons). It only states that the study “determine[s] the muscle innervation ratio exactly,” without explaining the ratio’s basis.",
        "The packet does not explicitly state that the innervation ratio is used to quantify “how much muscle reinnervation comes from the original nerve versus a donor nerve.” It reports findings such as UN-related reinnervation appearing in a specific group and donor-related efferent innervation being observed in a regenerating environment, but it does not directly support the original-vs-donor quantitative comparison claimed in the definition."
